:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=CRTWSCST.Create WSCST (CRTWSCST)
:P.Use the Create WSCST (CRTWSCST) command to compile a workstation
customizing object from a source member (the transform's commands for
one printer).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTWSCST/WSCST'.Workstation customizing object (WSCST)
:P.The workstation customizing object that describes the printer to the
host print transform.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTWSCST/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *WSCST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTWSCST/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SRCMBRTXT:EPK.
:PD.The text of the source member.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTWSCST/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QTXTSRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTWSCST/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBCRTAUT:EPK.
:PD.The create authority of the library the object is created in (CRTAUT
of the library).
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PK.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTWSCST/REPLACE'.Replace object (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTWSCST.Delete WSCST (DLTWSCST)
:P.Use the Delete WSCST (DLTWSCST) command to delete a workstation
customizing object.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTWSCST/WSCST'.Workstation customizing object (WSCST)
:P.The workstation customizing object that describes the printer to the
host print transform.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RTVWSCST.Retrieve WSCST (RTVWSCST)
:P.Use the Retrieve WSCST (RTVWSCST) command to write the customizing
source of a printer model into a source member, to change and compile
with CRTWSCST.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVWSCST/DEVTYPE'.Device type (DEVTYPE)
:P.The device type.
:P.A value is required.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TRANSFORM, *CTXFORM.
:P.The value must be 3101, 3151, 3161, 3162, 3163, 3164.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVWSCST/MFRTYPMDL'.Manufacturer type and model (MFRTYPMDL)
:P.The manufacturer type and model for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 15 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVWSCST/SRCMBR'.Source member (SRCMBR)
:P.The member of the source file that holds the source. *PGM, *MODULE or
*CMD and the like mean the member with the same name as the object being
created.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVWSCST/SRCFILE'.Source file (SRCFILE)
:P.The source physical file that holds the source member, by name and
library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, QTXTSRC is used.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RTVWSCST/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
